Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.81,0:00:04.98,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Hey, Omi?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.00,0:00:06.99,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Mm-ya?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.53,0:00:10.61,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,What we saw earlier... Whaddaya think it was?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.82,0:00:15.14,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Could be some kind of Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.14,0:00:17.71,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,You lose your Rights when you die,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.71,0:00:20.42,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,so someone else beside the \NEmperor might be behind it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.90,0:00:22.44,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,I thought so, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.44,0:00:25.46,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Sane and Saaya's bodies \Nwere perfectly preserved,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.46,0:00:28.43,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,and the Emperor's body was gone entirely.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.98,0:00:31.22,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,But who would do that? And why?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.30,0:00:35.07,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Good work, you two.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.07,0:00:37.28,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Sensei! I thought you were on watch duty.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.28,0:00:38.88,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,I had someone fill in for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.32,0:00:41.31,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,There's something \NI wanted to talk to you about.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.16,0:00:43.31,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,About what?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.89,0:00:45.54,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,It's about Raion...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.58,0:01:02.50,Show Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fad(250,0)\pos(320,110)}Tasuketsu: Fate of the Majority
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.99,0:02:18.16,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.77,0:02:22.55,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,So you failed in exterminating them \Nand ran back home.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.51,0:02:25.34,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,My sincerest apologies...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.53,0:02:28.38,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,No matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.66,0:02:33.60,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,At least we've gained some useful information \Nabout the Prime Right of Materialization.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.60,0:02:35.84,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,You're forgiven. However...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.69,0:02:39.71,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,Showing them your Water Utilization \Nwas a mistake.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.71,0:02:42.81,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,They'll have a strategy to kill you next time.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.72,0:02:48.05,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,If you don't want to die, come with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.05,0:02:50.35,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,I'll perform a ritual on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.86,0:02:52.28,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,But in return...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.72,0:02:57.05,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,Swear your eternal loyalty \Nto me. Over and over.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.95,0:03:01.49,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,About Raion?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.49,0:03:02.70,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,What's up?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.97,0:03:06.98,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,He's certainly reliable, but he's also \Neasily swayed by his emotions.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.50,0:03:12.53,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,I'm not sure it's wise to put him \Nin charge of strategies by himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.53,0:03:14.42,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,That was never the plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.14,0:03:18.05,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Besides, we don't want him \Nto take the fall like Saneatsu.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.30,0:03:22.18,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Well, he's definitely quick on his feet,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.18,0:03:24.99,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,so maybe we can just throw him \Ninto the line of fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.99,0:03:26.64,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,You're heartless.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.02,0:03:32.65,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,It's not ideal to be without a strategist, \Nbut we'll all just have to work together.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.75,0:03:36.61,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,Oh, almighty Queen, ruler \Nof the heavens and earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.61,0:03:39.67,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,Grant this powerless fool your \Ngreat love and benevolence.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.09,0:03:42.81,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,Oh, almighty Queen, ruler \Nof the heavens and earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.81,0:03:46.20,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,Grant this powerless fool your \Ngreat love and benevolence.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.20,0:03:49.29,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,Oh, almighty Queen, ruler \Nof the heavens and earth...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.11,0:03:56.26,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,There's a missing officer candidate, \NYoshiaki Hirayama.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.26,0:04:01.33,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,And another missing experiment \Nmember, Hikari Ebina.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.33,0:04:02.72,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,Since when?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.02,0:04:08.05,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,Attendance records show that both \Nhad returned as scheduled.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.05,0:04:13.51,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,But according to other members, Hikari \NEbina hasn't been back in over a month.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.79,0:04:16.78,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,Who recorded attendance?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.78,0:04:21.88,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,Hirayama, given that he was the most \Npromising of the candidates...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.03,0:04:28.08,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,Terminate all candidates \Nexcept the top three.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.08,0:04:29.59,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,As you wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.95,0:04:31.46,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,That saves us some hassle.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.07,0:04:33.28,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,As for you...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.71,0:04:38.97,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,Starting today, you'll have \Nthe Prime Right of Electricity.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.97,0:04:41.09,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,Thank you, my Queen...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.84,0:04:44.81,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,{\i1}Individuals can only possess one \NPrime Right and Right each....{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.81,0:04:47.53,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,{\i1}Once obtained, they can't be replaced.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.53,0:04:50.92,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,{\i1}But the Queen's powers flips \Nthat principle on its head.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.27,0:04:55.88,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,{\i1}The first of Lady Kisaragi's \Npowers is total control{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.88,0:04:58.47,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,{\i1}over the selection and obtainment of Rights!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.47,0:05:02.66,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,{\i1}As long as we serve Lady Kisaragi, \Nwe'll always have the upper hand!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.66,0:05:08.28,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,Ikusa, you'll be given more tasks \Nin the area of housing.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.28,0:05:10.04,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,I trust you'll work hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.05,0:05:13.58,Default,Ikusa,0,0,0,,Housing?! For what, milady?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.30,0:05:16.84,Default,Meguru,0,0,0,,Lady Kisaragi, I've brought you \Nthe candidates.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.02,0:05:22.59,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,Touya Mutsuki, Knight Kato, and Lili Kato.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.03,0:05:26.18,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,These are the top three officer candidates.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.18,0:05:30.18,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,Starting today, you three will be \Nsent to the front lines to fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.50,0:05:33.52,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,Don't disappoint me, Team Frontline.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.52,0:05:34.22,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,Yes, milady.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.22,0:05:35.64,Default,Knight,0,0,0,,Cool. Thanks, hag!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.64,0:05:37.52,Default,Lili,0,0,0,,Cut it out, Knight!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.99,0:05:42.64,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,Are you sure about this, Lady Kisaragi?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.64,0:05:44.79,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,Ikusa prefers to be on the battlefield.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.79,0:05:46.68,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,I don't believe he'll be happy...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.09,0:05:51.31,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,We must avoid informing the current \NEmperor of his new Prime Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.31,0:05:54.05,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,He'll be used when the time is right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.28,0:06:01.83,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,How I look forward to \Nthe day of our victory...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.83,0:06:04.29,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,At this pace, it shouldn't be much longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.29,0:06:07.26,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,What should I do first?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.25,0:06:11.62,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,Tell me... Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.66,0:06:18.70,Default,Man 1,0,0,0,,We got some great stuff today!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.70,0:06:22.35,Default,Man 2,0,0,0,,Nothing beats hunting down \Nsurvivors to steal food!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.35,0:06:23.91,Default,Takato,0,0,0,,Take a look, Yocchin!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.91,0:06:25.78,Default,Takato,0,0,0,,I bet there's double yesterday's amount!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.78,0:06:30.24,OS,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs30\frz27\fax0.6\pos(144,68)\c&H78BDDB&\bord3\3c&H2425C7&}The Emperors
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.78,0:06:30.24,Default,Woman,0,0,0,,Wow! We've been so lucky ever \Nsince Yohei became the leader!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.59,0:06:34.58,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,It may not be long before we \Nconquer this land as The Emperors...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.58,0:06:38.08,Default,Takato,0,0,0,,Standing up to the Emperor! \NYou're so cool, Yocchin!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.88,0:06:42.54,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,This pungent, foul stench,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.54,0:06:45.26,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,and these piercing, vulgar voices...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.62,0:06:50.14,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,Who the hell are you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.71,0:06:52.56,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,I'm the Cleaner.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.56,0:06:58.36,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,I exterminate civil waste for the Queen\N who will lead us into the ideal world.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.03,0:07:00.69,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,You'll be deleted.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.07,0:07:07.75,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,{\i1}W-what's going on?!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.75,0:07:09.81,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,{\i1}My body's so heavy...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.79,0:07:13.16,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,What the hell did you do?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.55,0:07:17.00,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,Get crushed, penetrate the earth, \Nand enrich the soil.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.47,0:07:21.82,Default,Takato,0,0,0,,It's so heavy...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.82,0:07:23.38,Default,Takato,0,0,0,,I-I'm gonna be crushed...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.84,0:07:26.26,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,Damn!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.05,0:07:29.23,Default,Woman,0,0,0,,Yohei! What did you do?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.81,0:07:41.06,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,I dunno what you did, \Nbut I'm not willing to die!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.44,0:07:44.15,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}This man... How is he moving?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.15,0:07:45.27,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,Die!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.27,0:07:46.53,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,Piss off!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.03,0:07:49.84,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}It rebounded!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.84,0:07:51.91,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}He must have some kind of Prime Right.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.31,0:07:55.44,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}All the more reason \Nto exterminate him here and now.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.44,0:07:57.54,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}I won't let anyone \Nget in Lady Kisaragi's way.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.52,0:08:09.60,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,Are you reinforcement?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.16,0:08:13.02,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,You... mentioned something about a Queen?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.02,0:08:15.27,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,I hope I'm not mistaken.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.52,0:08:18.37,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,I'm just excited to get more information.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.37,0:08:20.54,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,I'll delete anyone who stands in the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.54,0:08:23.01,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,Get crushed, penetrate the earth, and...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.01,0:08:24.19,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,Enrich the soil!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.05,0:08:33.66,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Hmm, I think I've got a good grasp \Nof your Prime Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.65,0:08:36.10,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}My Prime Right...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.10,0:08:39.83,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}The ability to control gravity \Nwithin a 10-meter radius.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.62,0:08:41.58,Comp very big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,28)}Gravity Right
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.83,0:08:41.00,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Prime Right of Gravity.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.91,0:08:45.50,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}Right now, he's standing in \Ngravity 50 times the usual force.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.50,0:08:49.48,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}Assuming he's about 60 kilograms, \Nthat would total a weight of 3 tons...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.48,0:08:52.59,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}And why are the glass shards floating?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.45,0:08:55.80,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll make it 100 times the usual force then!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.80,0:08:57.22,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}If that doesn't work...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.22,0:08:58.26,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,A thousand times!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.26,0:08:59.28,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,It's no use.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.73,0:09:03.86,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Did your Prime Right come \Nwith the definition of gravity?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.13,0:09:06.64,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}I knew it! He has a Prime Right too...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.64,0:09:08.25,Italics,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,No matter! Crush him!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.71,0:09:10.07,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,A thousand times the force!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.77,0:09:19.77,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,General relativity states that gravity is \Nthe result of distortions in time-space.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.77,0:09:21.62,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Were you aware of that?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.62,0:09:23.22,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's not working!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.22,0:09:25.96,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}Does his Prime Right neutralize \Nthe power of others?!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.54,0:09:31.51,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Perhaps it could be described as the energy \Nthat drains into these distortions.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.51,0:09:33.93,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Which would make countering them very easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.66,0:09:38.75,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Simply maneuver the direction \Nof energy to stop the force.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.41,0:09:42.80,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,As a result, gravity doesn't change one bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.80,0:09:44.77,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,This was a bad match-up for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.27,0:09:47.48,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,Get off your high horse...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.75,0:09:48.90,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,...and die!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.21,0:09:52.36,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,How's {\i1}that{\i0}!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.36,0:09:54.36,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Oh, my. Good for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.83,0:10:10.20,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,He flung back the ceiling I dropped on him?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.20,0:10:11.47,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,How is he alive?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.40,0:10:15.52,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Right behind you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.20,0:10:19.64,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,Why, you! Who are you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.05,0:10:22.91,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Listen, why don't we have a seat?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.29,0:10:26.71,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Let's have a nice chat after we capture you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.87,0:10:30.83,Show Title,,0,0,0,,{\pos(492,245)}Tasuketsu: Fate of the Majority
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.81,0:10:38.18,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}More reinforcements?! But when?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.18,0:10:39.79,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}How could he have— {\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.79,0:10:40.74,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}Don't tell me...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.08,0:10:45.11,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}That split second... \Nhe was hiding among the rubble?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.11,0:10:48.63,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}So he was waiting for that moment all along?!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.93,0:10:51.12,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}How could he make such \Na split-second decision?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.12,0:10:52.79,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}Or was it predetermined?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.18,0:10:55.36,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}But wait—that would mean...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.67,0:10:56.87,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}They read my moves?!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.87,0:11:01.85,Default,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,{\i1}You mean he knew I would drop the ceiling \Non him before he even appeared?!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.34,0:11:03.85,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Your call, Pres.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.85,0:11:05.56,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,You sure you want me to do it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.56,0:11:09.49,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Sure, go ahead. I'll adjust it accordingly.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.03,0:11:12.17,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Prime Right of...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.15,0:11:13.86,Comp very big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,28)}Explosion Right
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.17,0:11:13.61,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Explosion!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.07,0:11:20.59,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,I used my Prime Right of Induction \Nto lead the blast the other way.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.59,0:11:22.23,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Hey, you're right!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.23,0:11:24.37,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,This way, there's no damage to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.37,0:11:26.33,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,You're amazing, Pres!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.64,0:11:30.26,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,I think you'll eventually be able to \Ndo it yourself with some practice.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.26,0:11:34.47,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,But, man, how did you know he'd \Ndrop the ceiling on you beforehand?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.41,0:11:37.18,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,It's nothing complicated.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.62,0:11:41.98,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,If gravity itself won't work, there's \Nno choice but to use another method of attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.98,0:11:47.13,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Gravity works from the top down, so \Ndropping the ceiling is just the ticket.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.88,0:11:51.00,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Okay, but like... is he alive?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.00,0:11:54.19,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,He's alive. A few moments ago...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.19,0:11:56.29,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,I set my Suspension Right \Nso it would activate
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.29,0:12:00.53,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,when he felt his life was \Nin danger and halt time.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.53,0:12:01.84,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Oh yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.84,0:12:03.51,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,That's why you let him attack you!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.51,0:12:07.97,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Coincidence or not, we're lucky \Nto capture a suspect.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.97,0:12:09.83,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Now, shall we head home?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.39,0:12:13.00,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,But how will we carry him?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.90,0:12:19.68,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,Gravity is always at work.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.68,0:12:22.69,Default,Yagihashi,0,0,0,,My Induction Right can \Ncontrol anything, anytime.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.69,0:12:25.97,Default,Kazuhiko,0,0,0,,Man... You're like a cheater, Pres.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.44,0:12:35.47,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,That was cutting it close...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.49,0:12:38.72,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,Without this Prime Right, \Nthe Right of Transference,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.86,0:12:39.03,Comp very big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,28)}Transference Right
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.72,0:12:40.24,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,I'd be dead by now.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.57,0:12:43.85,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,And I used those guys as scapegoats...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.85,0:12:46.76,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,...by transferring them all the damage.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.33,0:12:49.26,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,This always happens.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.26,0:12:52.74,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,I always let go of the things \Nmost important to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.74,0:12:56.77,Default,Fukami,0,0,0,,I swore to stick by them \Nuntil the end... but still, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.33,0:13:00.10,Flashback,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,I'm the Cleaner.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.41,0:13:06.35,Flashback,Mutsuki,0,0,0,,I exterminate civil waste for the Queen\N who will lead us into the ideal world.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.60,0:13:10.46,Italics,Fukami,0,0,0,,The Queen... She's that bastard's boss!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.60,0:13:20.20,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Demoted?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.20,0:13:21.11,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Yup!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.11,0:13:24.42,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,We're not sure you're cut out for it, so \Nyou're demoted to Assistant Strategist!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.42,0:13:26.33,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Isn't that a bit too straightforward?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.92,0:13:32.19,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,But there's no Head Strategist, \Nso things will be decided by vote?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.19,0:13:33.88,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Okay, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.88,0:13:36.42,Default-Top,Gobo,0,0,0,,I'm playing my trap card!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.42,0:13:39.13,Default-Top,Nishime,0,0,0,,No, wait! I take it back!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.42,0:13:39.13,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,They seem way too comfortable...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.51,0:13:43.05,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,In times like these, \Nit's best to let loose a little.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.70,0:13:46.39,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Let's gather around for \Ntoday's strategy meeting.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.93,0:13:50.48,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,So we don't have any clue \Nas to the Queen's whereabouts...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.48,0:13:52.90,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,If you're not dead set on \Norganizing a preemptive attack,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.90,0:13:57.44,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,we could just wait for their first move \Nand prepare in the meantime.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.44,0:13:59.22,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,I vote nay to that!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.22,0:14:01.71,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Hard to prepare for anything
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.71,0:14:04.16,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,when we don't even know \Nthe first thing about their abilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.16,0:14:07.74,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Mm-yup, we'd need to know \Nwhat Rights they have...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.74,0:14:13.33,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(136,222)\fad(1,100)}Support
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.74,0:14:13.33,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,222)\fad(1,100)}Defense
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.74,0:14:13.33,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(490,222)\fad(1,100)}Offense
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.19,0:14:13.30,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Our primary offense is Ryuta, and \NOmi and Rika are our main defense.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.30,0:14:15.38,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Eren, Nishime, and I can act as support.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.46,0:14:20.13,White-Standard,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs20\fry25\fad(180,100)\b0\move(401,155,354,155,19,2855)}Death
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.94,0:14:20.13,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Souma's an all-rounder, but he can \Nonly materialize three times a day tops.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.19,0:14:23.93,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,So we're still a defense-heavy unit overall...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.93,0:14:27.69,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,You're right. We don't have much \Nof a chance without a striker.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.23,0:14:31.64,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Hey... this is a shot in the dark, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.03,0:14:34.45,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Why don't we try recruiting Ren Iruga?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.29,0:14:38.65,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,If he joins us, that's another striker \Nand we'll have better chances of winning.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.51,0:14:41.57,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Ren Iruga?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.43,0:14:45.11,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,He was originally our enemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.80,0:14:48.70,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,I think he had a change of heart \Nin the end, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.15,0:14:52.29,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,We have no clue where he went \Nafter defeating the Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.18,0:14:57.61,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,If he still has Gobo's communication device, \Nwe should be able to call him in.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.61,0:14:59.41,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Is he any good?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.36,0:15:03.63,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Of everyone we've seen... he's the strongest.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.36,0:15:06.55,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,So that settles that.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.55,0:15:08.85,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Could you send him a message?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.85,0:15:10.96,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,We already have, multiple times.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.96,0:15:13.73,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,I doubt it'll work, for real.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.73,0:15:15.73,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Not that I won't try, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.29,0:15:20.26,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Queen could already be on the move \Nwhile we're talking like this.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.26,0:15:23.46,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm sure they'll try to trace our footsteps.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.46,0:15:27.08,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}But we haven't left any, \Nso they won't have any leads.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.08,0:15:29.49,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}The question is... what to do then?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.42,0:15:32.83,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course! That'll be our play!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.63,0:15:35.33,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,Ya come up with an idea?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.33,0:15:39.96,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Yeah. We'll have to be assertive \Nif we want to edge out the Queen!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.46,0:15:42.16,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,So I'll lie!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.23,0:15:44.59,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,What did you just say?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.59,0:15:47.20,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,Touya Mutsuki is missing?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.20,0:15:49.24,Default,Meguru,0,0,0,,He left this morning to investigate,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.24,0:15:52.22,Default,Meguru,0,0,0,,but it's past his scheduled return \Nand he's nowhere to be found.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.63,0:15:55.93,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,I see. You can stand back.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.93,0:15:56.93,Default,Meguru,0,0,0,,Yes, milady.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.74,0:16:02.44,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,What do you think, Lady Kisaragi?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.81,0:16:05.66,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,Someone working for the \Ncurrent Emperor defeated him.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.66,0:16:07.70,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,It's safe to assume that's what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.80,0:16:13.54,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,We should act on the premise that they \Nnow know everything Mutsuki knows...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.16,0:16:18.18,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,Yes, perhaps we should leave here at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.92,0:16:22.72,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,Outside, Knight Kato will be the front guard.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.72,0:16:24.32,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,Meguru will be the rear guard.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.32,0:16:27.20,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,And inside, Lili Kato will be the front guard.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.20,0:16:29.18,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,And Ikusa will be the rear guard.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.18,0:16:32.80,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,I'll take Kou as my personal bodyguard, \Nand observe from afar.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.67,0:16:41.02,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,You impostor... I swear to you...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.37,0:16:42.52,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,I'll kill you!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.46,0:16:48.18,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,Lady Kisaragi, it's time for \Nthe Emperor's announcement.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.23,0:16:53.77,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's only so much they can do \Nwith mere text announcements.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.77,0:16:57.09,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,{\i1}The current Emperor's influence \Nwon't grow any greater.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.83,0:17:01.31,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,{\i1}I suppose I can check if they try \Nto probe us for any information...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.03,0:17:04.36,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,What could that be?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.34,0:17:06.80,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,I-It can't be!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.45,0:17:11.45,Italics,Voice,0,0,0,,Citizens across Japan, good evening. \NThis is your Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.30,0:17:15.67,Italics,Voice,0,0,0,,We will be commencing \NStage Three of Tasuketsu.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.31,0:17:19.43,Comp very big-an8,Sign,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,28)}National Instant Alert System
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.93,0:17:21.65,Italics,Queen,0,0,0,,The National Instant \NAlert System... JP-Alert!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.00,0:17:23.04,Italics,Queen,0,0,0,,Of course!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.04,0:17:25.57,Italics,Queen,0,0,0,,They used the Materialization \NRight for equipment!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.30,0:17:28.75,Italics,Voice,0,0,0,,There's only one rule to Stage Three:
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.75,0:17:31.96,Italics,Voice,0,0,0,,Capture the Queen who's hiding.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.66,0:17:34.45,Italics,Voice,0,0,0,,We will commence tomorrow at 10:00 AM.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.45,0:17:36.47,Italics,Voice,0,0,0,,Once someone succeeds,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.47,0:17:41.21,Italics,Voice,0,0,0,,all other participants will die as the \Nmajority being "unsuccessful participants".
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.56,0:17:50.73,Italics,Queen,0,0,0,,They used Stage Two of the real Tasuketsu \Nto their advantage and avoid any suspicion...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.25,0:17:53.97,Italics,Queen,0,0,0,,Dammit! At this rate...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.25,0:17:57.70,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,So they put you at the center \Nof Tasuketsu itself...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.70,0:18:00.07,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,Participants will assume \Nit's another game development
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.07,0:18:02.23,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,if you make an announcement yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.55,0:18:05.71,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,This will revive the Emperor's influence!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.07,0:18:09.35,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,No, something isn't right...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.43,0:18:13.94,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,This would unquestionably set off \Na killing spree among fools
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.94,0:18:17.31,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,who can't distinguish between \Nmyself and other participants...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.78,0:18:21.58,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,I highly doubt the current Emperor \Nwould do such a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.07,0:18:25.46,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,This is all a façade?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.46,0:18:29.42,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,Yes. And given the chance that they\Nhave knowledge of our location,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.42,0:18:34.22,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,this may be the current \NEmperor's first move to kill me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.22,0:18:39.10,Default,Kirishima,0,0,0,,Either way, I believe it's best we relocate.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.10,0:18:44.06,Default,Queen,0,0,0,,Yes, and we must gather information \Non them as soon as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.40,0:18:50.26,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,That was maybe your biggest lie yet, Raion.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.26,0:18:53.57,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,This way, we can make sure \Nthe Emperor still has authority.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.86,0:18:55.80,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,But now what?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.80,0:18:58.62,Default,Shinozaki,0,0,0,,Won't survivors start \Nkilling each other to find—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.62,0:19:00.48,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Nah, you'll see.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.95,0:19:05.29,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,I don't expect the general public \Nto be able to find the Queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.29,0:19:08.13,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,The Queen should know that much, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.13,0:19:13.26,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,I'm sure they want dirt on us, so hopefully\N they make a move one way or another.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.52,0:19:16.18,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,You sure we can act based on assumption?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.18,0:19:18.72,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Well yeah, we have no information to go off.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.72,0:19:20.54,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,If we guess right, then awesome.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.54,0:19:24.49,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,They're in the same boat as us... \Nwhich is exactly why I instigated first.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.49,0:19:28.52,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,I hope they'll come searching for \Nanywhere with the slightest chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.56,0:19:31.12,Default,Gobo,0,0,0,,Like KHN?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.12,0:19:34.24,Default,Nishime,0,0,0,,But... wouldn't they already \Nhave been there by now?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.24,0:19:37.26,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,There's one place I'm betting on.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.26,0:19:39.33,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,I'll tell you the details later,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.33,0:19:43.75,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,but I'm hoping we can come in contact \Nwith the Queen's troops there.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.39,0:19:47.21,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,That place is...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.88,0:19:55.55,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,So, why bet on the Emperor's tower?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.87,0:19:59.25,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,They've already figured out that \Nthe current Emperor's a fake, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.25,0:20:02.23,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Then what would they assume \Nabout the original Emperor?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.16,0:20:08.60,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Umm... they've been captured, they've \Ndied, or just somehow disappeared?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.05,0:20:10.73,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Yeah, so when?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.98,0:20:15.81,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Naturally, they'd assume something \Nhappened when Tasuketsu ended,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.81,0:20:20.01,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,and announcements changed from \Nvoice-overs to text announcements.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.67,0:20:23.73,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,So, that part's obvious.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.73,0:20:27.66,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,The only other question is how much \Nthe Queen knows about the Emperor's tower.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.36,0:20:30.86,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,The effects of the Concealment Right \Nhave worn off,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.86,0:20:33.17,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,and the tower is visible to anyone now.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.53,0:20:36.55,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,It wouldn't surprise me if \Nthe Queen came to see it herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.39,0:20:40.62,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,There's a chance she took \Nthe Emperor's body, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.17,0:20:43.05,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,Yeah, and another thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.05,0:20:46.98,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,One look inside and it's obvious \Nthere was a battle there.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.98,0:20:50.10,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,So whoever fought the Emperor...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.10,0:20:52.86,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,...would likely be the current Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.19,0:20:56.83,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,The tower is the only place the "real" Emperor \Ncame in contact with the "fake" Emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.83,0:21:01.05,Default,Raion,0,0,0,,And that makes it the best, and likely \Nonly, place to gather any information.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.05,0:21:03.98,Default,Omi,0,0,0,,I get it now! \NSo that's why you instigated!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.98,0:21:05.02,Default,Ryuta,0,0,0,,Get down!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.86,0:21:10.48,Default,Knight,0,0,0,,Man... this is such a drag \Nfirst thing in the morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.48,0:21:13.88,Default,Meguru,0,0,0,,What a brat! Stop complaining \Nand get to work, Knight!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.84,0:21:19.84,Next Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,The Lie
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.35,0:21:18.51,Default,Ryuta+Omi+Raion,0,0,0,,That's them!
